Subject: [PATCH] kbase: raise EXEC_VA zone from 16KB to 4MB

STATUS: HISTORICAL / ILLUSTRATIVE — see note below before trying to apply.

This diff was written by hand against an intermediate working state of
src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c (the file was saved as
"kbase_kmod.c.pre-exec-va-fix"), not against upstream Mesa. Its context
therefore does not match a clean checkout of the base commit
6598829019c0746aa8e473b4ae1c980cbfa6ea4b, and `git apply` will reject it there.

It is kept because it is the clearest single-purpose statement of the EXEC_VA
finding. **The applicable patch is
0013-panfrost-lib-kbase-and-fb-fixes.patch**, which contains this same
`va_pages = 1024` change against upstream, together with the EXEC_INIT/JIT_INIT
reordering it depends on.

The finding: KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_EXEC_INIT's va_pages is the size of the *entire*
EXEC_VA zone for all future executable allocations, not a per-call amount.
0x100000 was rejected EPERM on this device; 4 (16KB) passed EXEC_INIT but was
exhausted by internal overhead before the first compiled-shader allocation,
which then failed ENOMEM; 1024 (4MB) works.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,13 @@
    /* PATCH: EXEC_INIT dipindah SEBELUM JIT_INIT -- di device ini EXEC_INIT
     * gagal EPERM kalau ada operasi memori (termasuk JIT_INIT) yang jalan
     * duluan. */
-   struct kbase_ioctl_mem_exec_init exec_init = { .va_pages = 4 };
+   /* PATCH: va_pages=4 (16KB) was the minimum that passed EXEC_INIT itself,
+    * found by trial-and-error after 0x100000 (~4GB) was rejected. Turns out
+    * that's the *total* size of the EXEC_VA zone for all future executable
+    * allocations, not just the init call -- 16KB was immediately exhausted
+    * by the first real compiled-shader allocation (ENOMEM on
+    * KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_ALLOC with GPU_EX flag). Raised to 4MB. */
+   struct kbase_ioctl_mem_exec_init exec_init = { .va_pages = 1024 };
    if (ioctl(fd, KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_EXEC_INIT, &exec_init)) {
       mesa_logw("kbase: KBASE_IOCTL_MEM_EXEC_INIT failed: %s "
                 "(executable BO allocation will not work)", strerror(errno));
